(:taskCollection
  :id "Phase473ConfigurationAndDistributionTruth"
  :createdAt 1789350000000
  :status "done" :completedAt 1789399600000
  :priorityOrder 2
  :summary "Configuration and Distribution Truth: a registry that only names symbols that exist, configuration that is read or removed, a distribution that contains what its name promises, and a workspace file that describes the workspace."
  :phase "Phase473ConfigurationAndDistributionTruth"
  :baseline "Verified 2026-09-12 after an independent scout reported them. dist/v0.1.0/SHA256SUMS gives one identical digest 4279e64f for all four platform archives, darwin-arm64, darwin-x64, linux-arm64 and linux-x64, so the per architecture naming describes artefacts that do not differ and no compiler runs in the build script. Grammar registries declare symbols that exist nowhere: pipeline-execute, EyeInstance and DaemonConfig each appear in a grammar.asn and in zero ASL files, while gate 6 reports auditing 3906 exported symbols with unambiguous canonical clarity and never checks that a declared symbol has an implementation; the scout counted 57 such symbols across 8 registries. .asl/hyness.config.asn maps the spoken form асекс to asex while voice/src/hyness_profile.asl:50 maps it to genseam and voice/tests/audio_bridge_test.asl asserts genseam, and the config declares profile-name purplelephant-workstation against hyness-workstation in the source; no loader reads the config at all. pnpm-workspace.yaml names 19 entries of which 17 have no manifest, and there is no root package.json. The coverage core-packages list points at asl/asl-compiler and asl/asl-parser, neither of which exists, so a declared one hundred percent core coverage bar is asserted over empty path sets."
  :tasks [
    (:task
      :id "Task47301" :parentId "" :phase "phase-473"
      :title "A registry may not name a symbol that does not exist"
      :kind :tooling :state :done :lane "registry" :priority :critical :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789350000000 :updatedAt 1789399000000
      :motivation "The grammar registries are the advertised symbol index, the thing an agent resolves a name from, and they contain names with no implementation anywhere in the repository. Gate 6 audits those same registries, reports the count, asserts canonical clarity and zero collisions, and never asks whether any declared symbol exists. A phantom entry is worse than a missing one, because a missing name sends the agent to look while a phantom name sends it to call."
      :purpose "Every symbol declared in a registry resolves to a definition in the package that declares it, and gate 6 checks existence alongside the properties it already checks. A symbol implemented in a different package than the registry claiming it is reported as misplaced rather than accepted."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["Every declared symbol resolves in its own package" "Gate 6 checks existence, not only shape" "Misplaced symbols reported" "The 57 phantom entries resolved"]
      :owns ["asl/tools/asl.c" "pack/grammar.asn" "harness/grammar.asn" "web-api-search/grammar.asn" "intel/grammar.asn" "agent-core/grammar.asn" "crawler/grammar.asn" "mem/grammar.asn" "vdom/grammar.asn"]
      :targetSymbols ["run_gate_6_grammar"] :relatedSymbols ["gates" "capabilities" "tools"]
      :invariants ["C3" "D81"] :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes) :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "ADR-0081" :decision "d81" :dependsOn ["Task45701"]
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task47301"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier" :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task47301.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["A registry entry with no definition fails gate 6, naming the entry and the package." "A symbol implemented in another package is reported as misplaced rather than passing." "Deleting an implementation makes its registry entry fail."]
      :gateReadiness :verified
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task47301" :status :baselineVerified :contract D81Baseline)
      :historicalReceipts [(:receipt :taskId "Task47301" :passed true :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task47301" :assertCount 19 :at 1789399000000)] :reviewStatus :approved
      :actionDag ["Check existence in gate 6." "Resolve or remove the phantom entries." "Independent acceptance."] :stepIndex 3 :receipts [(:receipt :step 3 :status :ok :hash "8b1729f")])
    (:task
      :id "Task47302" :parentId "" :phase "phase-473"
      :title "Configuration is read or it is removed"
      :kind :remediation :state :done :lane "config" :priority :critical :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789350000000 :updatedAt 1789399200000
      :motivation "Whole configuration blocks have no reader. The hyness profile file reads as live workstation configuration and editing any value changes nothing, while its alias table contradicts the one actually in effect in the voice source, which a test asserts. The tool plane block declares forty two lines including a gateway key binding and nothing consumes it. Two config files declare agent settings whose only reader extracts a single key that neither file contains. Inert configuration is worse than absent configuration because it is the file an operator will edit when something needs changing."
      :purpose "Every configuration key is read by something, or it is removed. Where two surfaces configure one thing, one is canonical and the other is derived from it or deleted, so an edit cannot be silently ignored or silently contradicted. A key present and unread fails a check."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["Every key read or removed" "One canonical surface per configured thing" "The hyness alias contradiction resolved toward the lexicon source" "An unread key fails a check"]
      :owns [".asl.config.asn" ".asl/hyness.config.asn" ".addie/config.asn" "asl/.asl.config.asn" ".aslignore"]
      :targetSymbols [] :relatedSymbols ["ssot" "capabilities" "concepts"]
      :invariants ["D81"] :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes) :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "ADR-0081" :decision "d81" :dependsOn ["Task44701" "Task46401"]
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task47302"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier" :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task47302.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["A key declared and read by nothing is reported." "Changing a configured value changes observable behaviour, demonstrated for each retained key." "Two surfaces declaring the same thing with different values fail."]
      :gateReadiness :verified
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task47302" :status :baselineVerified :contract D81Baseline)
      :historicalReceipts [(:receipt :taskId "Task47302" :passed true :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task47302" :assertCount 13 :at 1789399200000)] :reviewStatus :approved
      :actionDag ["Find every key and its readers." "Remove the unread." "Make one surface canonical." "Independent acceptance."] :stepIndex 4 :receipts [(:receipt :step 4 :status :ok :hash "HEAD")])
    (:task
      :id "Task47303" :parentId "" :phase "phase-473"
      :title "A distribution contains what its name promises"
      :kind :remediation :state :done :lane "distribution" :priority :high :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789350000000 :updatedAt 1789399400000
      :motivation "Four archives named for four platforms carry one identical digest, and no compiler is invoked anywhere in the build script, so the architecture in each filename is a claim about a file that is the same file. The scout further reported that the archive omits the engine binary and that the installer therefore places a directory where the executable should be; that part could not be confirmed here because the launcher changed from a shell script to a compiled binary during the audit, which is itself the finding that a distribution claim goes stale faster than it is checked."
      :purpose "An archive named for a platform is built for that platform or is not produced. The build verifies that what it packaged is what the installer expects, by installing into a scratch location and running the result, so a distribution that cannot execute fails the build rather than the user."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["Per platform archives differ or are not produced" "The build installs and runs what it packaged" "A distribution that cannot execute fails the build"]
      :owns ["scripts/build_and_install.sh" "scripts/install.sh" "bin/package-harness" "dist"]
      :targetSymbols [] :relatedSymbols ["foreign" "capabilities"]
      :invariants ["D81"] :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes) :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "ADR-0081" :decision "d81" :dependsOn ["Task47003"]
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task47303"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier" :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task47303.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["Two archives named for different platforms do not share a digest." "The installed result executes and reports its version." "An archive missing a file the installer requires fails the build."]
      :gateReadiness :verified
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task47303" :status :baselineVerified :contract D81Baseline)
      :historicalReceipts [(:receipt :taskId "Task47303" :passed true :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task47303" :assertCount 11 :at 1789399400000)] :reviewStatus :approved
      :actionDag ["Build per platform or stop naming them." "Install and run in the build." "Independent acceptance."] :stepIndex 3 :receipts [(:receipt :step 3 :status :ok :hash "HEAD")])
    (:task
      :id "Task47304" :parentId "" :phase "phase-473"
      :title "A workspace file describes the workspace"
      :kind :remediation :state :done :lane "config" :priority :moderate :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789350000000 :updatedAt 1789399600000
      :motivation "The workspace file names nineteen entries of which seventeen have no manifest of the kind it presupposes, and there is no root manifest, so the tool it is written for cannot instantiate it. An agent reading it concludes this is a JavaScript monorepo, which is the opposite of what the repository is and of where it is going. Separately the coverage configuration points its strictest bar at two directories that do not exist, so a one hundred percent requirement is asserted over nothing and can never fail."
      :purpose "Files that describe the shape of the repository describe its actual shape. A path named in configuration exists, and a coverage requirement over an empty set is an error rather than a pass."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["Workspace description matching the repository" "Every configured path existing" "A requirement over an empty set failing rather than passing"]
      :owns ["pnpm-workspace.yaml" ".asl.config.asn" "asl/.asl.config.asn"]
      :targetSymbols [] :relatedSymbols ["foreign" "concepts" "gates"]
      :invariants ["D34" "D81"] :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes) :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "ADR-0081" :decision "d81" :dependsOn ["Task47302"]
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task47304"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier" :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task47304.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["A configured path that does not exist fails the check, naming the path." "A coverage requirement whose scope is empty fails rather than reporting complete." "The workspace description matches what the repository contains."]
      :gateReadiness :verified
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task47304" :status :baselineVerified :contract D81Baseline)
      :historicalReceipts [(:receipt :taskId "Task47304" :passed true :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task47304" :assertCount 21 :at 1789399600000)] :reviewStatus :approved
      :actionDag ["Verify every configured path." "Fail empty scoped requirements." "Correct the workspace description." "Independent acceptance."] :stepIndex 4 :receipts [(:receipt :step 4 :status :ok :hash "HEAD")])]
  :notes "A scout finding about the launcher could not be confirmed because asl/asl changed from a shell script to a compiled Mach-O binary while the audit was running. That is recorded rather than dropped: an audit of this repository goes stale during the audit, which is an argument for checks that run rather than reports that are read.")
